"consumer product" means an article, substance, preparation, or device that is supplied for personal, domestic, or household use, and includes any component part or accessory;

"supply" includes supply by way of sale, exchange, lease, hire, or hire-purchase;

"the Minister" means the Commonwealth Minister responsible for consumer affairs;

"the Chair" means the Chair of the Commission appointed under Part 4;

"the Deputy Chair" means the Deputy Chair of the Commission appointed under Part 4;

"the CEO" means the Chief Executive Officer appointed under Part 5;

"enabling legislation" means the legislation under which the Commission is established and operates, as amended from time to time.

1.3.2 A reference to a Part or clause is a reference to a Part or clause of this Charter unless the context otherwise requires.

1.3.3 A reference to a person includes a body politic or corporate and a reference to a gender includes every other gender.

**PART 2 – OBJECTS AND FUNCTIONS**

**2.1 Objects**

2.1.1 The primary object of the Commission is to protect the safety of consumers in Australia by reducing the risk of injury, illness, or death associated with consumer products.

2.1.2 The Commission shall pursue this object through a combination of:

a) monitoring and analysing product safety information and data;

b) identifying emerging product safety hazards;

c) coordinating product safety activities with Commonwealth, State, and Territory agencies;

d) providing advice and recommendations to the Minister; and

e) promoting public awareness of product safety issues.

**2.2 Functions**

2.2.1 The Commission has the following functions:

a) to monitor the safety of consumer products supplied in Australia;

b) to collect, analyse, and disseminate information relating to product safety;

c) to investigate, either on its own initiative or in response to a complaint, any matter relating to the safety of a consumer product;

